requirements.on options: doublet: each geothermal doublet; heat_pump: each heat pump; boiler: each boiler; chp: each combined heat and power unit; chiller: each chiller; heat_exchanger: each heat exchanger; heating_supply: the heat delivered to the consumers; cooling_supply: the cold delivered to the consumers; plant: the whole plant
requirements.quantity options: count: how many units of the role there are: a number of units, never days; production_flow: brine flow of a doublet; brine_cooling: brine temperature drop from producer to injector; production_temperature: brine temperature at the producer; injection_temperature: brine temperature at the injector; pump_power: electric power of a doublet's pumps; pump_efficiency: hydraulic efficiency of a doublet's pumps; intake_pressure: pressure at the pump intake; intake_gas_fraction: free gas share at the pump intake; reinjection_ratio: injected over produced brine volume; wellhead_pressure: pressure at the wellhead; cop: coefficient of performance; lift: temperature lift of a heat pump; heat_output: heat a unit gives; cold_output: cold a unit gives; duty: heat a heat exchanger transfers; approach: smallest temperature difference of a heat exchanger; fuel_input: fuel a unit burns; power_output: electric power a unit gives; unmet: demand not covered; unmet_share: share of the demand not covered, 0-1; temperature: temperature delivered; co2: CO2 emitted; electricity_bought: electricity bought; gas_bought: gas bought; gas_burned: gas burned; heat_surplus: heat made beyond the demand
Operating days are a time, never a count: `{name: running_time_limit, on: doublet, quantity: production_flow, over: duration, when: running, max: <days>, unit: d}`; a number of doublets is `{on: doublet, quantity: count, min, max}`.

